    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2963,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 682,
      "heading": "Everything you need to audit your DI container.",
      "backgroundColor": "#14110D",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "Everything you need to audit your DI container. Drop-in observability with zero ceremony. Drop-in Setup One line: do.NewWithOpts(plugin.Opts()). Zero config, zero ceremony. Dependency Graph Infers which service resolved which — forward and reverse — without touching do's internals. Scope Tree Full hierarchy with per-scope service lists, cross-scope resolution tracked automatically. 16+ Export Formats JSON, NDJSON, CSV, TSV, HTML, Mermaid, PlantUML, DOT, D2, tree, and table. Health Check Audit Wraps injector.HealthCheck() with per-service events and unhealthy-service detection. ~1.7us Overhead ",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3645,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 640,
      "heading": "Try it in 30 seconds.",
      "backgroundColor": "#14110D",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Copy",
        "Browse the example source"
      ],
      "text": "Try it in 30 seconds. Clone the repo and run the self-checking example. Copy $ DO_AUDITLOG_ENABLED=true go run ./example === Audit Summary === Container: ride-share-app Services: 20 Events: 145 Scopes: 4 Build: 0.128ms HTML: audit-report.html The example exercises every major samber/do v2 feature - eager and lazy providers, named services, transients, aliases, child scopes, cross-scope dependencies, health checks, and shutdown errors - then writes an HTML report you can open in any browser. ✓ 20 services across 4 scopes ✓ Dependency graph inference ✓ Health checks & shutdown errors ✓ Self-cont",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4284,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 584,
      "heading": "How it works.",
      "backgroundColor": "#14110D",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "How it works. Three steps from zero to full observability. 1 Create the Plugin Pass plugin.Opts() to do.NewWithOpts. Hooks fire on every registration, invocation, and shutdown. 2 Run Your Container The plugin captures events in memory with an invocation stack that infers the dependency graph. 3 Export & Visualize Get a JSON snapshot, NDJSON event stream, or a self-contained HTML page. Or render Mermaid, DOT, D2, PlantUML.",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4869,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 656,
      "heading": "Why do-auditlog?",
      "backgroundColor": "#14110D",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "Why do-auditlog? Purpose-built for samber/do v2 observability. DIY DIY ✗ No built-in hooks consumer ✗ Manual timestamp wiring ✗ No dependency graph inference ✗ No export formats do-auditlog Free ✓ One-line setup ✓ Auto-inferred dependency graph ✓ 16+ export formats including HTML ✓ Health check audit ✓ Real-time event streaming Manual Manual ✗ Hand-roll logging per service ✗ No visualization ✗ No replay or migration ✗ Maintenance burden",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
